    "field": "High-altitude climate change",
    "problem": "Existing studies on altitude-dependent temperature change provide conflicting conclusions, a problem hampered by the scarcity of long-term, homogenous high-altitude observations and the incompatibility of data from different sources like surface stations versus free-atmosphere measurements.",
    "method": "The author investigates the altitude dependency of climate change by calculating and comparing linear temperature trends from long-term records of 56 high- and low-altitude meteorological stations, assembled into 18 regional groups across 10 major mountain ranges.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the altitude dependency of temperature change by analyzing historical temperature data from major mountain ranges worldwide, and to explain the physical reasons for the observed enhanced warming variability at higher elevations.",
